From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: fontview, the Fonts folder, per-user fonts, shell: URLs

Windows has fontview.exe in system32 and a Fonts folder; Wine has neither.
sg-shell's sg-fontview is both (App Paths fontview.exe). This patch is what
Wine itself needs for them:

- programs/fontview: fontview.exe (system32 and syswow64) is calc's
  launcher (0120's handoff.c) for what App Paths registers for it.
- wine.inf: .ttf/.otf/.ttc/.fon open in fontview.exe, with Windows'
  "Install" and "Install for all users" verbs (no-clobber).
- win32u: a user's own fonts load -- HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows NT\
  CurrentVersion\Fonts ("Name (TrueType)" = the file's full path), as
  Windows 10 1809 installs fonts per user without an administrator. Wine
  read only HKLM's key, so a per-user font was invisible to every program.
- explorer: the Fonts folder (shell:fonts, its CLSID, or %WINDIR%\Fonts)
  opens the Fonts view of the program App Paths names for fontview.exe
  (`/folder`), or the plain folder when there is none. shell:<known folder>
  opens that folder (IKnownFolderManager::GetFolderByName) instead of being
  sent back through ShellExecute, and wine.inf registers the shell: URL
  scheme to explorer -- Wine had none, so the Run box's shell:fonts,
  shell:downloads ... failed.

Gate: test/fonts-gate.sh.
